  "body": "Although it's certainly no longer recommended for use (the `id` attribute took its place), there was a `name` attribute of the `<a>` element which created an anchor in the same way `id` does, and I imagine this is still a requirement for implementations even though the feature is obsolete. It isn't mentioned anywhere in the `<a>` element's description, though. I would expect this to be defined there, and if WHATWG decided not to spec it for some reason, to mention in a note why.\r\n\r\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/text-level-semantics.html#the-a-element\r\nhttps://www.w3.org/TR/html4/struct/links.html#h-12.2",
